{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Neighbouring amenity",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development would result in the loss of a dwellinghouse capable of accommodating a family with children. This would be detrimental to the borough&#x27;s stock of these type of dwellings, the identified local need for which is set out in the Development Plan Policies and supporting evidence. The provision of two smaller units is not considered sufficient to justify the harm to the Borough&#x27;s family housing stock. The harm caused by way of a reduction in the borough&#x27;s supply of dwellinghouses capable of accommodating families with children significantly and demonstrably outweighs the benefits of the proposed flats. As such, the proposal would conflict with the following policies which seek to ensure that the borough&#x27;s housing supply meets the needs of its residents: &lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024);&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; Policies H1 &amp;amp; H2 of the London Plan (March 2021); &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Policies SPDG1, SP3 and DMH5 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;"
  ],
